<h2>🏢 2. Many-to-Many Organizational Mappings</h2>

<h3>Project ↔ Project Manager (PM) Mappings</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Project Unilever (UI)</strong>: Assigned to David Chen (Primary) and Sarah Connor (Backup).</li>
  <li><strong>Project P&G (PG)</strong>: Assigned to Sarah Connor (Primary) and David Chen (Backup).</li>
  <li><strong>Project PepsiCo (PEP)</strong>: Assigned to Alex Kim (Primary) and David Chen (Backup).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Super Manager ↔ Project Manager (PM) Mappings</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Maria Santos (super.fmcg@...)</strong>: Supervises David Chen (Unilever) and Sarah Connor (P&G).</li>
  <li><strong>John Miller (super.retail@...)</strong>: Supervises Alex Kim (PepsiCo) and Sarah Connor (P&G).</li>
</ul>

<h2>✉️ 3. Field Approver Escalation Paths</h2>
<p>Field Approvers evaluate candidate submissions directly from email via secure single-use 1-click links (zero portal login needed):</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Level 1 (PM Approval)</strong>: Project Manager email (e.g. pm.unilever@recruitment.local).</li>
  <li><strong>Level 2 (Area Sales Manager - ASM)</strong>:
    <ul>
      <li>Default fallback: abhishek.gopale@idonneous.com</li>
      <li>Chicago Metro Area Override: chicago.asm@company.com</li>
      <li>Atlanta Metro Area Override: atlanta.asm@company.com</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Level 3 (Regional Sales Manager - RSM)</strong>:
    <ul>
      <li>Default fallback: abhishek.gopale@idonneous.com</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>🚀 4. Step-by-Step Testing Guide</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Log In as Project Manager:</strong> Go to <a href="http://localhost:5173">http://localhost:5173</a> and log in as <code>pm.unilever@recruitment.local</code> / <code>Pm@123456</code>. Inspect dynamic roles and the duplicate triage queue.</li>
  <li><strong>Log In as Recruiter North:</strong> Log in as <code>recruiter.north@recruitment.local</code> / <code>Recruiter@123456</code>. View the Instagram-style card feed with SLA countdown badges and submit a candidate.</li>
  <li><strong>Review Rejection Loop:</strong> Use the rejection form to test structured feedback. Notice the vacancy immediately resets to ACTIVE with the manager's notes.</li>
</ol>

